  "visualBrief": "Detached Utrecht DomTower: native two square stages and open octagonal lantern. Deep continuous pointed ground passage with layered portal moldings/ribbed soffit and own ground-following paving. Warm brick blind Gothic niches/pale stone quoins, glazed lower lights/physical galleries with pierced pointed/trefoil tracery and crocketed pinnacles. Four green skeletal square clocks/gold Roman rings/hands, real second-stage pointed openings/physical mullions/louvers/iron ties. Giant two-light lantern sections/stone tracery band/deep molded arches/corner buttresses/gables/upper green railing. Short slate/lead octagonal cap/cross and original gilded SaintMartin horseman vane. No cathedral nave/choir/visitorreception/neighbors/scaffold/interior bell machinery.",
